  "body": "This 1950s brick home has been transformed through an extensive, no-expense-spared renovation and is now seeking a new custodian. \r\n\r\nPositioned on an elevated, private, freehold site, this home, on one of Auckland's most prized streets, had been extended and adapted over time. The current owners continued that evolution, with a new, redesigned kitchen, renovated bathrooms and extensive improvements to the outdoor spaces and gardens.\r\n\r\nFrom the covered balcony the outlook reaches across the water and back towards Auckland's skyline, offering an active, expansive outlook and particularly beautiful sunsets. Wide folding doors connect the balcony to the main living and dining rooms, opening much of this level to the outdoors.\r\n\r\nPolished timber floors draw the living spaces together. Designed by Wendy Shacklock Architects, the kitchen combines curved detailing, warm timber tones and brushed metallic accents. A full butler's pantry provides a separate space for preparation and serving, with extensive storage. A breakfast nook sits to one side, while a family room connects the kitchen with the private, sheltered garden courtyard.\r\n\r\nHere, mature planting encloses an outdoor dining space beneath louvres, with a fireplace at one end. The setting feels intimate, with greenery close to the table and doors opening back into the family room. A discreet gate offers a secondary access point from the driveway into the home for those requiring flat, level access. \r\n\r\nOn the level below, manicured gardens frame the swimming pool and paved terraces, with a timber deck providing space to lounge beside the water.\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms and four bathrooms are thoughtfully configured to include two bedroom suites on separate levels, each complete with a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite. The principal suite enjoys direct access to the pool terrace, complemented by a renovated ensuite with a freestanding bath. A second suite provides an ideal retreat for guests or extended family.  \r\n\r\nSeparate office, double garaging with internal access and dedicated storage complete this offering.\r\n\r\nFOUND: UNDERSTATED ELEGANCE ON PARITAI.\r\n\r\nPlease note, this home may qualify under the Active Investor Plus (AIP) Visa.",
